  "usage_note": "A bus usually has a **stop**: a place by the road, often with only a sign. A **station** is a larger place, often with a building, where buses or trains start, stop, and wait. In British English, **full stop** is also the name of the mark (.) at the end of a sentence; American English calls it a **period**.",
  "learner_errors": [
